      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "У нас французский ресторан.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a French restaurant.' Barinov storms up to Kristina to remind her that Claude Monet is a French restaurant.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "А не японский.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And not Japanese.' He stresses that they are not a Japanese sushi bar.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я обожаю суши.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I adore sushi.' Kristina shrugs off his culinary pride and says she simply adores sushi.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я ем их каждый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I eat them every day.' Since she eats sushi every day, she wants it on her restaurant's menu too.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "А если ты захочешь хачапури?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what if you want khachapuri?' Viktor sarcastically asks what happens if she suddenly craves Georgian cheese bread tomorrow.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я вызову хачапурщика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will call a khachapuri maker.' Missing the sarcasm, Kristina replies that she would just hire a khachapuri baker.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я умею готовить хачапури.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I know how to cook khachapuri.' Senya pipes up from the side to brag that he knows how to bake khachapuri.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Заткнись и пошёл вон.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Shut up and get out.' Furious at the interruption, Barinov snaps at Senya to shut up and get lost.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "С тобой невозможно разговаривать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is impossible to talk to you.' Turning back to Kristina, Viktor groans that reasoning with her is impossible.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Кстати, Вика у нас не работает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'By the way, Vika doesn't work for us.' Kristina casually drops the news that Vika no longer works at the restaurant.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "barinov",
      "t": "Ты её уволила?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you fire her?' Shocked, Viktor asks if Kristina fired their art director.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Она сама уволилась.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She quit herself.' Kristina stretches the truth, claiming that Vika decided to quit on her own. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
